```plaintext
Scene Description in RDF Triples (Turtle Format)
```

```turtle
@prefix ex: <http://example.org/autonomous-driving#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

ex:Scene1 a ex:DrivingScene ;
    ex:timeStamp "2023-10-05T23:45:30"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    ex:location "Urban residential area" .

ex:Pedestrian1 a ex:Pedestrian ;
    ex:location ex:Scene1 ;
    ex:position "Crosswalk, near center of image" ;
    ex:clothingColor "Yellow top, light grey pants" ;
    ex:action "Crossing road" .

ex:Vehicle1 a ex:Vehicle ;
    ex:location ex:Scene1 ;
    ex:position "Foreground, partially visible, bottom of image" ;
    ex:vehicleType "Autonomous car" ;
    ex:action "Driving" .

ex:StreetLight1 a ex:StreetLight ;
    ex:location ex:Scene1 ;
    ex:position "Background, left side of image" ;
    ex:status "On" .

ex:Building1 a ex:Building ;
    ex:location ex:Scene1 ;
    ex:position "Right side of image" .

ex:Road1 a ex:Road ;
    ex:location ex:Scene1 ;
    ex:surfaceCondition "Wet" ;
    ex:roadType "Urban residential street" .

ex:Relationship1 a ex:Relationship ;
    ex:subject ex:Vehicle1 ;
    ex:predicate ex:approaching ;
    ex:object ex:Pedestrian1 .

ex:Relationship2 a ex:Relationship ;
    ex:subject ex:Pedestrian1 ;
    ex:predicate ex:crossing ;
    ex:object ex:Road1 .

ex:WeatherCondition1 a ex:WeatherCondition ;
    ex:location ex:Scene1 ;
    ex:condition "Nighttime" ;
    ex:visibility "Low due to darkness" .
```

```plaintext
Identified Risks for each risk class
```

**Risk 1:**
Description: Pedestrian crossing the road in front of an autonomous vehicle during nighttime with low visibility.
Severity Score: 0.95

**Risk 2:**
Description: Wet road surface increasing the risk of skidding or reduced braking efficiency for the autonomous vehicle.
Severity Score: 0.75

**Risk 3:**
Description: Potential occlusion of the pedestrian by the vehicle itself due to the low angle and position of the camera, which might hinder the vehicle's sensors from detecting the pedestrian in time.
Severity Score: 0.85

**Risk 4:**
Description: Nighttime conditions reducing the effectiveness of visual sensors and increasing the reliance on other detection methods (e.g., LiDAR, radar).
Severity Score: 0.80

**Risk 5:**
Description: Limited visibility of the pedestrian's full body and movements due to the angle and lighting, which could lead to misinterpretation of the pedestrian's intentions.
Severity Score: 0.82

These risks highlight the importance of robust sensor fusion and adaptive algorithms in autonomous vehicles to handle low-visibility scenarios effectively.